.SH BUGS
At most 16 machines and 8 vCPUs each.  A machine's memory is one
contiguous run of host memory: no ballooning or overcommit.
.PP
VMX: no VPID, so the TLB is flushed on every entry and exit.  A
guest's debug registers DR0\-DR3 and DR6 are kept and read back but
not loaded, so its hardware breakpoints do not fire.  No APIC
virtualization or posted interrupts (VMX), nor AVIC (SVM): every
interrupt is injected.  Guests cannot run hypervisors of their own.
.PP
Assignment: memory BARs only, MSI-X only, no extended configuration
space, and only a function the host has no driver for.  A function
without FLR that shares its bus is released blocked but not reset.
An assigned function's interrupt raised on another processor is
seen at the vCPU's next exit, at most a clock tick later.
.PP
A machine cannot be saved, restored or moved: the platform's devices
have no state files, and the kvmclock records are not rewritten
across a stop.
.PP
No XSAVE state beyond x87/SSE is offered to guests.
.PP
.B "traps sys"
is x86 only so far, and its system calls are Inferno's, not Linux's.
